#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:120
msgid "Passkey: A secret stored on a device, unlocked with biometrics."
msgstr ""
"Klucz dostępu: sekret zapisany na urządzeniu i odblokowywany "
"biometrycznie."

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:129
msgid ""
"Alternative challenge message to use when authenticating with a "
"passkey.You can also use tags for replacement, check the documentation "
"for more details."
msgstr ""
"Niestandardowy komunikat wyzwania używany podczas uwierzytelniania "
"kluczem dostępu. Można używać znaczników do automatycznego zastępowania. "
"Więcej informacji zawiera dokumentacja."

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:135
msgid ""
"When enabled, passkey token can be triggered with the PIN or via the "
"/validate/triggerchallenge endpoint. For privacyIDEA plugins, this is not"
" recommended. It is advised to use a condition, for example on a user-"
"agent, with this policy."
msgstr ""
"Po włączeniu token klucza dostępu można wyzwalać za pomocą PIN-u lub "
"przez endpoint /validate/triggerchallenge. Nie jest to zalecane w "
"przypadku wtyczek privacyIDEA. Z tą polityką zaleca się użycie warunku, "
"np. dotyczącego nagłówka User-Agent."

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:142
msgid ""
"Only allow authentication with passkeys reporting a specific device type,"
" given as a space-separated list of 'single_device' and/or "
"'multi_device'. A single_device credential is not backed up (typically a "
"hardware security key or a non-syncing platform authenticator), a "
"multi_device credential is backed up and can be used on several devices "
"(a synced/cloud passkey). This is verified cryptographically on every "
"authentication, not just at enrollment. By default both types are "
"accepted."
msgstr ""

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:152
msgid ""
"Require that the userHandle returned by the authenticator matches the "
"FIDO2 user ID that was recorded for the user when the passkey was "
"enrolled. By default, privacyIDEA identifies the user solely via the "
"credential ID and its assignment to a user in privacyIDEA, so a passkey "
"that is unassigned and then assigned to a different user will "
"authenticate as that different user. Enabling this detects such a "
"reassignment for regular clients, at the cost of the authentication "
"failing for any passkey that was enrolled before this attribute was "
"recorded. Note that, unlike the device type, the userHandle is not "
"covered by the WebAuthn assertion signature: it is a safeguard against an"
" unintended reassignment, not a defense against a client that "
"deliberately sends a forged value."
msgstr ""

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:168
msgid ""
"Request attestation from the authenticator during the registration. The "
"attestation certificate will be saved in the token info. The default "
"value is 'none'."
msgstr ""
"Żądaj atestacji od urządzenia uwierzytelniającego podczas rejestracji. "
"Certyfikat atestacji zostanie zapisany w informacjach o tokenie. Wartość "
"domyślna: 'none'."

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:175
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The name of the passkey that the authenticator shows in the credential "
"selection during login (and during registration). Use this to tell "
"passkeys apart, e.g. when the same login name exists in several realms. "
"You can use the tags {user} (login name), {realm}, {resolver} and "
"{serial}, as well as any attribute the user's resolver provides (e.g. "
"{givenname}, {surname}, {email}), for replacement, e.g. '{user}@{realm}'."
" The resolved value is also used as the display name. Unknown tags "
"resolve to an empty string and the result is limited to 64 bytes. If the "
"value is empty or the policy is not set, the login name of the user is "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:187
msgid ""
"Restrict passkey enrollment to authenticators reporting a specific device"
" type, given as a space-separated list of 'single_device' and/or "
"'multi_device'. A single_device credential is not backed up (typically a "
"hardware security key or a non-syncing platform authenticator), a "
"multi_device credential is backed up and can be used on several devices "
"(a synced/cloud passkey). The device type is reported by the "
"browser/authenticator and cannot be requested up front, so enrollment is "
"rejected afterwards if it does not match. By default both types are "
"accepted."
msgstr ""

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:597
msgid "Please authenticate with your passkey!"
msgstr "Uwierzytelnij się kluczem dostępu!"

#: lib/tokens/passkeytoken.py:601
msgid "Please confirm the registration with your passkey!"
msgstr "Potwierdź rejestrację kluczem dostępu!"

#: lib/tokens/passwordtoken.py:112
msgid ""
"A token with a fixed password. Can be combined  with the OTP PIN. Is used"
" for the lost token scenario."
msgstr ""
"Token ze stałym hasłem. Można go połączyć z PIN-em tokena. Jest używany w"
" procedurze utraconego tokena."

#: lib/tokens/passwordtoken.py:124
msgid "The user may only have this maximum number of password tokens assigned."
msgstr "Maksymalna liczba tokenów hasłowych, które można przypisać użytkownikowi."

